[META]
framework: claude-framework
file_id: backlog.LIFECYCLE
class: universal
version: 1.0.0

[LIFECYCLE]
overview: Statuses a backlog item can hold and legal transitions between them
principle: Transitions are explicit. Agent may perform some autonomously; others require user approval. Every transition is appended to the item's HISTORY section.

[STATUSES]
proposed:
  meaning: Item captured but not yet reviewed by user
  entered_from: (initial state on capture)
  agent_may_set: YES — default on capture
  user_sees: Listed when user asks "what's in the backlog?"

accepted:
  meaning: User has reviewed and confirmed the item should be done eventually
  entered_from: proposed
  agent_may_set: NO — requires user action (user says "accept BL-042" or "yes, do it later")
  note: Accepted items are what enters planning/prioritization discussions

in-progress:
  meaning: Item is actively being worked on via the workflow module
  entered_from: accepted (preferred), proposed (if user activates directly), deferred
  agent_may_set: YES — triggered by OPERATIONS.activate
  concurrency: At most 3 items in-progress at once; warn user if they request a 4th

done:
  meaning: Work is complete and verified (workflow REPORT phase succeeded)
  entered_from: in-progress
  agent_may_set: YES — on successful REPORT phase of the linked workplan
  immutable: HISTORY locks here; no further transitions (except to archive)

deferred:
  meaning: Temporarily paused; will return to accepted/in-progress later
  entered_from: accepted, in-progress
  agent_may_set: NO — requires user to say so (or agent proposes and user confirms)
  note: Use when user says "put this on hold" or "not this sprint"

rejected:
  meaning: Decided not to do it (invalid, obsolete, wrong-fix)
  entered_from: proposed, accepted, deferred
  agent_may_set: NO — requires explicit user decision
  immutable: Terminal; not deleted so the history is preserved

[TRANSITION_MATRIX]
# Rows = from, Columns = to. Cells = who can trigger.
#
#             proposed  accepted  in-progress  done    deferred  rejected
# proposed    —         user      user         —       user      user
# accepted    —         —         agent/user   —       user      user
# in-progress —         user      —            agent   user      user
# done        —         —         —            —       —         —       (terminal)
# deferred    —         user      user         —       —         user
# rejected    —         —         —            —       —         —       (terminal)
#
# Transitions marked `agent` fire automatically when the corresponding event happens.
# Transitions marked `user` require the user to explicitly say so; agent may propose but not execute.

[AGENT_AUTONOMOUS_TRANSITIONS]
These happen without asking the user:
  - (initial) → proposed            — on capture
  - accepted → in-progress          — when user runs OPERATIONS.activate BL-XXX
  - in-progress → done              — on workflow REPORT phase success for the linked workplan

All other transitions require a direct user instruction. Agent MAY propose a transition in a message
(e.g. "BL-042 looks obsolete — reject?") but MUST NOT execute it without the user's explicit "yes".

[CONCURRENT_IN_PROGRESS_POLICY]
Hard cap: 3 items in-progress simultaneously.
  - Prevents context thrash and half-finished work
  - On attempt to start a 4th: "Already 3 items in progress: BL-X, BL-Y, BL-Z. Defer one first, or pick a replacement?"
  - This is a soft-gate handled at OPERATIONS.activate time

[TRANSITIONS_AND_EXTERNAL_SYNC]
If the item has `LINKS.external_id` set and sync_target is non-none:
  - Local transitions do NOT automatically push to the external tracker
  - Sync is explicit — see SYNC.toon
  - Agent MUST note in the message: "Local status updated. Run sync to propagate to <tracker>."

[HISTORY_ENTRY_FORMAT]
Every transition appends ONE line to item's [HISTORY] section:
<ISO datetime> — <old_status> → <new_status> — <reason or trigger>

Examples:
  2026-04-18T10:15:00Z — (initial) → proposed — source: spawn_task
  2026-04-19T09:02:00Z — proposed → accepted — user: "ok, do this eventually"
  2026-04-20T14:30:00Z — accepted → in-progress — OPERATIONS.activate, workplan=add-webhook-retries
  2026-04-20T17:45:00Z — in-progress → done — workflow REPORT success
